     ssnndd__vviiaa88223333 — VIA Technologies VT8233 bridge device driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ssoouunndd
           ddeevviiccee ssnndd__vviiaa88223333

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           snd_via8233_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssnndd__vviiaa88223333 bridge driver allows the generic audio driver, sound(4),
     to attach to the VIA VT8233 audio devices.  These audio chipsets are in‐
     tegrated in the southbridge on many VIA based motherboards.

   RRuunnttiimmee CCoonnffiigguurraattiioonn
     The following sysctl(8) variables are available in addition to those
     available to all sound(4) devices:

           _d_e_v_._p_c_m_._%_d_._p_o_l_l_i_n_g  Experimental polling mode, where the driver op‐
                               erates by querying the device state on each
                               tick using callout(9).  Polling is disabled by
                               default.  Do not enable it unless you are fac‐
                               ing weird interrupt problems or if the device
                               cannot generate interrupts at all.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The ssnndd__vviiaa88223333 driver supports the following audio chipsets:

     ••   VIA VT8233
     ••   VIA VT8233A
     ••   VIA VT8233C
     ••   VIA VT8235
     ••   VIA VT8237
     ••   VIA VT8251

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     sound(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ssnndd__vviiaa88223333 device driver first appeared in FreeBSD 4.7.

